  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.6.0\n- Add opt-in unsafe generated accessors for callers that guarantee valid padded buffers.\n- Add allocation-free contiguous and strided batch primitives plus generated batch accessors.\n- Isolate source generation per bit object and resolve backing storage through Roslyn symbols.\n- Support nullable byte arrays, escaped identifiers, compatible derived attributes, and fully qualified generated references.\n- Add BITSKIT007-BITSKIT014 diagnostics for invalid generator options, layouts, names, backing fields, pointers, and modifiers.\n- Fix nonzero-offset array-backed accessors and unsafe raw-pointer generation.\n\nv1.5.0\n- Add sequential BitStreamWriter support for non-seekable compression, encryption, and network streams.\n- Generate direct mask-and-shift scalar accessors for integral, enum, and Boolean fields.\n- Specialize aligned Memory, Span, array, and byte InlineArray accessors plus common 11-, 12-, 24-, and 48-bit fields.\n- Accelerate buffered stream operations while preserving seeking, EOF, and in-place behavior.\n- Add normalized generated-accessor benchmarks and an original-version performance regression workflow.\n- Fix signed integral-backed Boolean getters.\n\nv1.4.0\n- Make stream reads reliable across partial reads and fail cleanly at EOF.\n- Add pooled sequential buffering for BitStreamReader and BitStreamWriter.\n- Preserve in-place writes and support stream positions beyond Int32.MaxValue.\n- Improve aligned UInt32 stream writes by about 15% and mixed unaligned writes by about 6% in local benchmarks.\n\nv1.3.1\n- Fix tag-driven GitHub Release creation in the split release pipeline.\n\nv1.3.0\n- Establish community-maintained releases under the RejectKid.BitsKit package ID.\n- Add .NET 10 support while retaining existing library targets.\n- Add reproducible builds, dependency locking, and automated package validation.\n- Fix incremental source-generator caching and restore the BITSKIT003 diagnostic.\n- Fix inline-array setters for modern C# compiler span overload resolution.\n- Remove EOL .NET 6 and .NET 7 targets and modernize test and benchmark dependencies.\n- Add categorized local and automated benchmark reporting for the library's features.\n\nv.1.2.0\n- Support InlineArrays.\n\nv.1.1.0\n- Add contracts to IO classes.\n- Support Readonly Instance Members.\n- Support Integral Type Casting.\n\nv.1.0.0\n- Initial release.",
